# PRIVATE lab repository (budzinskilab). Tracks our own code, our
# results and the presentation deck. NOT tracked: HCP-derived input data,
# the source papers' code releases (pang2023_BrainEigenmodes, Vohryzek2024),
# the PDF article library, and result files over 50 MB (GitHub's limits;
# listed below and in the README).
#
# Strategy: ignore everything by default, then explicitly un-ignore the
# specific files/folders that are our own code or docs.

/*

# --- Root-level scripts and docs ---
!/*.m
!/README.md
!/.gitignore
!/Project Update.pptx

# --- Our own code folders ---
!/functions/

# --- Our results (figures and .mat outputs) ---
!/results/

# --- Result files over 50 MB: too large for GitHub, kept local only (see README) ---
/results/EDR_LR_connectome_full_resolution.mat
/results/step4_5_full_resolution_reconstruction.mat

# Never track local editor/session settings or stray OS files anywhere
.claude/
.DS_Store
